  "id": "COMPOUND:34725 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Agallochin F is implicated in the pathogenesis of SCCH-26 through a multi-step mechanism involving protein tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The evidence suggests that Agallochin F acts as a target for a protein tyrosine phosphatase, which in turn is targeted by a compound with the structure [(1S,2S,6R,7R,9R,10S,11S,12R,14S)-11-hydroxy-14-methyl-5-methylidene-4-oxospiro[3,13-dioxatetracyclo[8.4.0.02,6.012,14]tetradecane-9,2'-oxirane]-7-yl] (E)-4-hydroxy-2-methylbut-2-enoate. This compound is also a target of 5-Fluorouracil1-acetic acid hydrazide, which further links to SCCH-26. The integrated evidence suggests that Agallochin F may exert its effects through a pathway involving protein tyrosine phosphatase inhibition, potentially modulating cellular signaling in SCCH-26 cells. The presence of multiple targets and their downstream effects supports a mechanistic link between Agallochin F and SCCH-26, though the exact mode of action and the role of the secondary targets remain to be fully elucidated.",
